WEBVTT

00:00.797 --> 00:02.717
[birds chirping]

00:08.727 --> 00:09.847
Hmm.

00:09.977 --> 00:12.647
Hey, Cliff, it's me.
Open up, will ya?

00:13.607 --> 00:15.977
[ELINALISE] It's not locked.
Come on in.

00:16.567 --> 00:17.687
[RUDEUS] Hmm?

00:24.577 --> 00:26.287
Oh, were you here by yourself?

00:26.407 --> 00:27.367
Yeah.

00:27.497 --> 00:28.957
Cliff went back
out to the church

00:29.077 --> 00:30.577
to do more prep for the wedding.

00:31.417 --> 00:32.787
[RUDEUS]
Cliff proposed to Elinalise

00:32.917 --> 00:34.497
before we left for Begaritt,

00:34.627 --> 00:35.917
and she said yes.

00:36.047 --> 00:38.007
It's still hard to believe.

00:38.127 --> 00:40.127
Elinalise settling down?

00:40.677 --> 00:43.507
Ah, of course.
That's coming right up.

00:43.637 --> 00:44.887
[sighs]

00:45.307 --> 00:47.307
Uh-oh, what's
that heavy sigh all about?

00:47.427 --> 00:49.977
Oh, nothing. He's just so busy.

00:50.097 --> 00:52.307
He's had no time
to get busy with me.

00:52.437 --> 00:53.517
[laughs sheepishly]

00:53.647 --> 00:54.977
But once your love nest
is ready,

00:55.107 --> 00:57.067
we're not gonna see you guys
for weeks.

00:57.187 --> 00:58.277
[sighs]

00:58.397 --> 01:00.737
Delayed gratification
is not my favorite.

01:00.857 --> 01:04.117
How I envy you, bedding two
lovely wives at the same time.

01:04.237 --> 01:05.777
Wait, don't say it like that!

01:05.907 --> 01:07.577
It's not like we're having
threesomes or anything.

01:07.697 --> 01:09.997
What? That surprises me.

01:10.497 --> 01:13.877
Doing it with a group can be
a wonderful bonding activity.

01:13.997 --> 01:15.917
You ought to try it
at least once.

01:16.037 --> 01:17.047
[gulps]

01:17.627 --> 01:18.797
No, don't listen to her!

01:18.917 --> 01:20.717
That's the devil
whispering in your ear!

01:20.837 --> 01:22.177
Just try bringing that up
and watch

01:22.297 --> 01:24.757
both of your relationships
crumble to dust!

01:24.887 --> 01:26.257
Be strong, Rudeus!

01:26.387 --> 01:28.137
Begone, foul temptress!

01:28.257 --> 01:29.467
You know,

01:29.767 --> 01:32.017
I wouldn't mind laying some
groundwork with the two of them

01:32.137 --> 01:33.807
if that would take
some of the pressure off.

01:33.937 --> 01:36.307
I beseech thee,
O great Elinalise!

01:36.437 --> 01:37.897
My goodness.

01:38.027 --> 01:39.437
Yes, I can do that for you,

01:39.567 --> 01:41.397
but I don't work
for free, you know.

01:41.527 --> 01:42.817
[groans]

01:43.147 --> 01:44.277
Right. Sure.

01:44.407 --> 01:46.817
So what can I do
for you in return?

01:46.947 --> 01:49.287
[chuckles] I've heard about
a prized aphrodisiac

01:49.407 --> 01:50.327
in the Asura Kingdom

01:50.447 --> 01:52.157
that I'd love
to get my hands on.

01:52.287 --> 01:55.207
Honestly, I'm surprised
that you would even need it.

01:55.537 --> 01:57.587
A little something special
for the wedding night.

01:57.707 --> 02:00.127
I want my husband
to come at me like a beast.

02:00.257 --> 02:01.207
[RUDEUS] Hmm.

02:01.917 --> 02:03.217
Yeah, fair enough.

02:03.337 --> 02:05.217
I'll see what I can do
to procure some.

02:05.337 --> 02:06.337
[giggles]

02:06.427 --> 02:08.597
To think of my sweet Cliff
losing control

02:08.717 --> 02:10.807
makes me absolutely feral.

02:12.427 --> 02:15.597
[♪ opening theme song playing]

02:23.447 --> 02:25.777
[PRIEST] Do you, Cliff Grimoire,

02:25.907 --> 02:29.277
vow to love Elinalise Dragonroad
as your wife

02:29.407 --> 02:31.287
so long as you both shall live?

02:31.407 --> 02:34.497
Yes, I do,
until the very end of my days.

02:35.037 --> 02:37.877
Good. And do you,
Elinalise Dragonroad,

02:38.247 --> 02:40.747
vow to love Cliff Grimoire
as your husband

02:40.877 --> 02:42.507
so long as you both shall live?

02:42.627 --> 02:43.797
Absolutely.

02:43.917 --> 02:46.167
I will love you
with everything that I am.

02:46.297 --> 02:47.337
Hmm.

02:48.217 --> 02:50.807
Then let the groom
present his bride

02:50.927 --> 02:53.267
with the necklace of Millis.

02:54.727 --> 02:56.597
Uh, Lise,
could you bow your head for me?

02:56.727 --> 02:58.687
Oh! Of course, my love.

02:59.147 --> 03:00.567
[necklace clinks]

03:02.647 --> 03:05.397
[PRIEST] You may give the groom
the promissory kiss.

03:05.527 --> 03:06.817
Gladly.

03:18.747 --> 03:22.287
O God! Bless these two souls
with eternal love,

03:22.417 --> 03:25.377
that they may live
in everlasting prosperity.

03:41.397 --> 03:42.817
Wasn't that amazing?

03:42.937 --> 03:45.567
He was so handsome,
and she's so pretty.

03:45.687 --> 03:48.027
I know.
I'd love a dress like that.

03:48.157 --> 03:49.407
That sure got their attention.

03:49.527 --> 03:51.657
Do all girls dream
of weddings like that?

03:52.027 --> 03:53.277
Well, some do.

03:53.407 --> 03:55.787
Although, our wedding
was so homey and quiet,

03:55.907 --> 03:58.037
and I thought that was
pretty much perfect for us.

03:58.167 --> 03:59.077
I agree.

04:02.917 --> 04:03.957
Hmm?

04:07.007 --> 04:09.427
Would you wanna throw
a big event like this?

04:09.927 --> 04:10.887
No.

04:11.427 --> 04:13.637
[RUDEUS] Roxy and I
didn't have a wedding at all.

04:13.757 --> 04:16.307
Apparently,
it's just not a Migurd custom.

04:16.927 --> 04:19.477
Still, after attending one,

04:19.597 --> 04:22.057
she might be inclined
to change her mind.

04:22.477 --> 04:24.397
I don't need a ceremony
or anything,

04:24.517 --> 04:27.487
but I guess I just want...

04:30.567 --> 04:31.907
[chuckles]

04:35.787 --> 04:36.827
Huh?

04:38.197 --> 04:41.207
Pardon me. Your forehead
is just so beautiful.

04:41.327 --> 04:43.327
Oh. No, that's okay.

04:43.457 --> 04:44.327
[chuckles]

04:44.627 --> 04:47.127
Rudy, you got one of those
for me too?

04:50.587 --> 04:51.587
[giggles]

04:52.087 --> 04:53.717
Okay, that's enough.

04:53.837 --> 04:55.557
We get it, you're married too.

04:55.677 --> 04:57.767
You don't have to go
smooching in public.

04:57.887 --> 04:59.887
Are you feeling left out?

05:00.017 --> 05:03.647
Hey, no! No public smooching.

05:07.067 --> 05:09.317
Ugh, you're so embarrassing.

05:09.437 --> 05:11.447
Time and place, Big Brother.

05:11.567 --> 05:12.607
Aisha?

05:14.027 --> 05:15.277
Big Brother!

05:15.407 --> 05:16.527
[both chuckle]

05:18.197 --> 05:21.787
Young lady, don't latch onto him
with your legs like that.

05:21.907 --> 05:22.867
[AISHA] Oh, fine.

05:22.997 --> 05:24.287
My word, Aisha.

05:24.417 --> 05:26.497
You're 11 years old,
for goodness' sake.

05:26.627 --> 05:28.337
You know better
than to jump around like that

05:28.457 --> 05:29.587
while you're wearing a dress.

05:29.707 --> 05:32.177
It's okay.
We're all family here.

05:32.717 --> 05:34.507
Wait, 11?

05:34.637 --> 05:35.547
I got a kiss...

05:36.007 --> 05:37.597
I don't think we ever celebrated
their fifth birthdays,

05:37.717 --> 05:39.387
much less their tenth.

05:40.557 --> 05:42.517
Paul wouldn't have had a chance
during the fallout

05:42.637 --> 05:44.517
from the teleportation incident.

05:45.147 --> 05:46.147
Don't be.

05:46.517 --> 05:48.607
And how about you host
the party when we get home?

05:49.817 --> 05:51.237
[RUDEUS] Well, that settles it.

05:51.987 --> 05:53.817
Let's have us a party.

05:55.907 --> 05:57.617
[♪ festive music playing]

05:58.697 --> 06:00.247
[lively chatter]

06:03.327 --> 06:05.167
[ROXY] The city
is always so lively

06:05.287 --> 06:06.167
around this time of year.

06:06.287 --> 06:07.247
[SYLPHIETTE] Isn't it?

06:07.377 --> 06:08.917
The harvest festival
brings people in

06:09.047 --> 06:10.127
from all over the place.

06:10.257 --> 06:11.707
And there couldn't be
a better time

06:11.837 --> 06:14.177
to shop for presents with all
the interesting, rare stuff

06:14.297 --> 06:15.757
that gets brought in
from abroad.

06:15.887 --> 06:18.217
I know. I'm excited
to see what we find.

06:18.807 --> 06:20.807
[RUDEUS] I'm throwing the girls
a surprise party,

06:20.927 --> 06:23.557
and I needed Sylphie and Roxy
to help me pull it off.

06:24.347 --> 06:27.517
But that's not the only reason
we're out on the town today.

06:27.647 --> 06:29.397
Elinalise came through for me.

06:29.517 --> 06:32.817
As promised, I've gone
and laid the groundwork for you.

06:33.357 --> 06:35.147
[chuckling]

06:35.277 --> 06:37.277
[SYLPHIETTE] Rudy? Rudy?

06:38.027 --> 06:39.407
Are you okay?

06:39.527 --> 06:40.947
You're drooling everywhere.

06:41.077 --> 06:43.197
Maybe we should go ahead
and get a bite to eat, huh?

06:43.697 --> 06:45.457
[RUDEUS] Woof,
I'm getting ahead of myself.

06:45.577 --> 06:47.247
Can't get sloppy about our date.

06:47.377 --> 06:49.537
We'll pick out some gifts
for Norn and Aisha,

06:49.667 --> 06:52.087
and then I stoke
the flames of love.

06:52.207 --> 06:53.797
Both are equally important.

06:53.917 --> 06:54.967
Sorry about that.

06:55.087 --> 06:57.177
Lost in thought,
and my jaw went slack.

06:57.297 --> 06:59.177
Now then, shall we?

07:01.637 --> 07:02.637
Look here,

07:03.177 --> 07:05.687
this pot freezes its contents
when it's imbued with mana.

07:05.807 --> 07:08.057
You think Aisha'd appreciate
something like this?

07:08.187 --> 07:09.477
It's good for the house,

07:09.557 --> 07:11.767
but she might like something
a little cuter for her room.

07:11.897 --> 07:13.437
Oh, that's a good point.

07:13.567 --> 07:14.777
For Norn, though,

07:14.897 --> 07:16.987
I don't even know
where to begin with that one.

07:17.107 --> 07:18.737
She's pretty studious.

07:18.867 --> 07:20.067
Something for school?

07:20.317 --> 07:23.117
[ROXY] She seems to like all
the same things that boys do.

07:23.247 --> 07:25.247
Armor and swords
and horses and stuff.

07:25.367 --> 07:27.787
That's true.
Surprised you knew that.

07:27.917 --> 07:29.127
Well, you know,

07:29.247 --> 07:31.707
I'd like to make better friends
with her if I can.

07:33.417 --> 07:34.707
[RUDEUS] Hmm.

07:35.167 --> 07:36.457
Oh.

07:50.357 --> 07:51.317
Hmm?

07:51.437 --> 07:52.477
[coins clink]

07:52.977 --> 07:54.317
[gasps]

07:55.357 --> 07:56.397
[sighs]

08:01.117 --> 08:02.907
[footsteps]

08:03.027 --> 08:04.657
[indistinct chatter]

08:06.787 --> 08:07.997
[SYLPHIETTE]
Thanks for helping me

08:08.117 --> 08:09.037
pick out some new clothes

08:09.157 --> 08:10.377
on top of everything else.

08:10.497 --> 08:11.957
Of course. Don't mention it.

08:12.077 --> 08:13.837
I had a lot of fun
with you today.

08:14.707 --> 08:16.587
It's about time
for dinner, you know.

08:16.877 --> 08:17.967
-Huh?
-Uh.

08:18.087 --> 08:20.797
I, uh, made some reservations.

08:24.307 --> 08:25.757
[SYLPHIETTE] I know this place.

08:25.887 --> 08:28.227
My grandmother
was telling me about it.

08:28.347 --> 08:30.517
She said this would be
a good place to make up

08:30.637 --> 08:32.477
if we ever had a fight.

08:32.607 --> 08:35.607
Oh, yeah?
She told me about it too.

08:35.727 --> 08:37.027
Although, in a little more of a,

08:37.147 --> 08:39.197
"This would be a nice getaway
for all three of you,"

08:39.317 --> 08:41.817
kind of way,
for some alone time.

08:43.117 --> 08:45.447
Oh, wait, alone time.

08:45.577 --> 08:46.867
She meant...

08:48.537 --> 08:50.407
I should have guessed.

08:51.537 --> 08:53.957
Rudy, you're shameless.

08:54.087 --> 08:55.037
[RUDEUS]
Say what you will about me,

08:55.167 --> 08:56.747
but you married this.

08:56.877 --> 08:58.757
Besides, it was
Elinalise's idea, not mine.

08:58.877 --> 08:59.837
I really owe her.

09:00.167 --> 09:02.217
[SYLPHIETTE] Oh! We can't spend
the night tonight.

09:02.337 --> 09:03.257
What about Lucie?

09:03.637 --> 09:05.717
Not to worry,
I already talked to Lilia.

09:05.847 --> 09:06.887
She's got her covered.

09:06.967 --> 09:09.387
[SYLPHIETTE] Did you?
Well, in that case,

09:09.517 --> 09:11.887
I know she'll be
in good hands at least.

09:12.437 --> 09:14.187
[RUDEUS] Sylphie probably
doesn't like the idea

09:14.307 --> 09:16.187
of us both being gone overnight.

09:16.687 --> 09:18.737
Maybe I shouldn't have
sprung this on them.

09:18.857 --> 09:19.857
But...

09:20.317 --> 09:21.987
Nah, I won't make excuses.

09:22.527 --> 09:24.237
I'm sorry, sweet Lucie.

09:24.367 --> 09:27.487
Forgive your father
for caving to his desires.

09:28.327 --> 09:30.747
Now then, ladies.

09:30.867 --> 09:32.327
-Rudy.
-Oh, here we go.

09:34.537 --> 09:35.957
I got a room.

09:37.627 --> 09:40.467
So, uh, join me upstairs?

09:40.587 --> 09:43.257
[chuckling] Oh, yeah,
I always wanted to say that.

09:43.717 --> 09:44.757
[BOTH] Uh.

09:46.797 --> 09:47.927
Mm.

09:48.057 --> 09:49.807
I know we talked about it,

09:49.927 --> 09:51.637
but just to make extra sure,

09:51.767 --> 09:53.847
you are okay
with doing this together?

09:53.977 --> 09:56.437
Oh, yes. I think I'm prepared.

09:56.557 --> 09:58.397
I trust both of you completely.

10:01.397 --> 10:03.947
[chuckling excitedly]

10:07.527 --> 10:10.077
This is going to be
a night to remember.

10:13.617 --> 10:14.827
[birds chirping]

10:15.327 --> 10:17.667
-[footsteps]
-[door opens]

10:18.997 --> 10:21.627
Today's the day
of the surprise birthday party.

10:22.087 --> 10:24.467
Sylphie's going to help Lilia
decorate and cook,

10:24.587 --> 10:25.887
but first and foremost,

10:26.007 --> 10:29.097
Roxy and I need to
get my sisters out of the house.

10:29.217 --> 10:31.427
[sweeping]

10:33.097 --> 10:34.137
[thuds]

10:47.277 --> 10:48.987
Oh, you're all in here!

10:49.117 --> 10:50.987
Hey, Norn, Roxy, Aisha.

10:51.117 --> 10:52.327
I'd like a word.

10:52.447 --> 10:53.957
Would you come with me, please?

10:54.077 --> 10:55.457
About what exactly?

10:55.577 --> 10:56.787
That sounds great.

10:56.917 --> 10:58.167
We can all go with you.

10:58.287 --> 10:59.207
Huh?

10:59.377 --> 11:01.507
Master Rudeus
is inviting you out, dear.

11:01.627 --> 11:03.627
Go on. You can tag along.

11:04.167 --> 11:06.177
[AISHA, NORN] Uh... Huh?

11:06.927 --> 11:08.547
[stream flowing]

11:11.137 --> 11:12.387
[gasps excitedly]

11:14.927 --> 11:15.887
So, we're fishing?

11:16.017 --> 11:16.977
Yeah.

11:17.307 --> 11:19.807
Seems like a good
family bonding activity, right?

11:23.277 --> 11:26.067
Norn still acts standoffish
around Roxy,

11:26.487 --> 11:28.737
and Roxy said she wanted
to try and win her over.

11:29.527 --> 11:32.657
So, hopefully
this will do the trick.

11:35.617 --> 11:38.627
You know, I've never
actually fished before.

11:38.747 --> 11:40.377
I never have either.

11:41.337 --> 11:43.917
It is something I've always
wanted to try, though.

11:45.297 --> 11:46.667
[both gasp]

11:46.797 --> 11:48.087
What do you think?

11:48.337 --> 11:50.847
Wanna compete and see which one
of us can catch the most fish?

11:50.967 --> 11:53.097
Uh, yeah, if that's
what you wanna do.

11:53.217 --> 11:54.177
How about this?

11:54.467 --> 11:56.597
Whoever loses has to do
whatever the winner says.

11:56.727 --> 11:57.597
You're on!

11:57.727 --> 11:59.137
[chuckling]

11:59.267 --> 12:01.107
Mm. Uh...

12:01.807 --> 12:04.767
Uh, hey, Brother,
what do I do with this stuff?

12:04.897 --> 12:05.987
[Rudeus laughs]

12:06.647 --> 12:08.487
I wish I knew what to tell ya.

12:08.607 --> 12:11.067
To be honest,
I've never gone fishing either.

12:13.027 --> 12:14.117
[ROXY] Um...

12:16.747 --> 12:19.327
If you'd like,
I'd be happy to teach you.

12:21.667 --> 12:23.707
[NORN] Oh. Yes, I'd like that.

12:25.627 --> 12:27.797
[ROXY] You wanna slide the worm
onto the hook

12:27.917 --> 12:29.297
without tearing it.

12:30.427 --> 12:32.597
We should cast our lines
towards the opposite bank,

12:32.717 --> 12:33.927
just underneath those trees.

12:34.047 --> 12:34.887
[water splashes]

12:35.007 --> 12:36.097
Think you can do it?

12:36.557 --> 12:38.017
[NORN] I'll give it a shot.

12:45.017 --> 12:46.017
[grunts]

12:47.647 --> 12:49.567
You're pretty good at this.

12:49.987 --> 12:51.407
Thank you for saying so.

12:51.527 --> 12:53.367
Ah. [grunts]

12:55.617 --> 12:57.367
I wish I could do that.

12:57.497 --> 12:59.207
When I was traveling alone,

12:59.327 --> 13:00.577
to survive, I had to be able

13:00.707 --> 13:03.287
to catch my own food
as often as possible.

13:04.127 --> 13:05.207
[grunts]

13:05.337 --> 13:06.417
[water splashes]

13:11.467 --> 13:13.047
[NORN] That reminds me.

13:13.177 --> 13:14.757
When we traveled with Ruijerd,

13:14.887 --> 13:17.557
he used to catch tons of fish
for us like it was nothing.

13:17.677 --> 13:18.807
[ROXY] He fishes too?

13:18.927 --> 13:20.887
[NORN] No,
not like we are, anyway.

13:21.017 --> 13:22.687
He would jab his spear
into the water

13:22.807 --> 13:25.517
and pull it back out
with three fish on the tip.

13:25.647 --> 13:28.277
Oh, look at that, Norn!
You've got yourself a bite!

13:28.397 --> 13:29.277
Huh?

13:29.397 --> 13:31.147
-Try pulling it.
-Right! Yeah.

13:33.817 --> 13:35.157
-[gasps]
-[grunts]

13:35.277 --> 13:36.157
[Norn grunts]

13:36.277 --> 13:37.867
That's it, just like that.

13:37.987 --> 13:38.907
Now pull!

13:39.037 --> 13:41.457
Hang in there. Easy does it.

13:41.577 --> 13:43.917
[Norn straining]

13:44.037 --> 13:45.827
-Ah!
-[both grunt]

13:50.047 --> 13:51.377
[both chuckle]

13:51.507 --> 13:54.297
Hey, look! Roxy,
I caught my first fish!

13:55.007 --> 13:57.217
[ROXY] Oh, wow! A big one too!

13:57.347 --> 13:58.427
[both laughing]

13:58.557 --> 13:59.807
[RUDEUS] It was
only a matter of time

13:59.927 --> 14:01.347
until they warmed up
to each other.

14:01.477 --> 14:02.767
There we go. [chuckles]

14:02.887 --> 14:04.687
And that makes three. [chuckles]

14:08.897 --> 14:10.437
Aw, what's wrong?

14:10.567 --> 14:11.777
You getting mad?

14:11.897 --> 14:14.107
Mad because your little sister's
whooping you?

14:14.237 --> 14:15.527
'Cause I'd be upset too.

14:16.157 --> 14:17.487
How could this happen to me?

14:17.617 --> 14:19.327
I wonder what
I should make you do.

14:19.447 --> 14:21.657
What if I had you cuddle me
all night, whispering,

14:21.787 --> 14:22.707
"Aisha, Aisha,

14:23.207 --> 14:25.667
you're the cutest little girl
in the whole wide world"?

14:26.377 --> 14:28.627
[RUDEUS] I mean, I guess
I could live with it.

14:28.957 --> 14:29.997
Screw that!

14:30.207 --> 14:31.837
I'm the man of the house,
her big brother.

14:31.957 --> 14:32.967
I can do better.

14:33.917 --> 14:35.297
[grunts]

14:35.427 --> 14:38.047
Here we go!

14:38.177 --> 14:40.137
All right, it's a big...

14:40.257 --> 14:41.847
[birds chirping]

14:42.887 --> 14:44.097
Not a fish.

14:44.227 --> 14:46.347
We must keep
our fishing spots clean.

14:46.477 --> 14:47.857
It's a fisherman's duty.

14:48.857 --> 14:50.977
Aisha, I'm about to get serious.

14:51.107 --> 14:53.487
Does that mean
you weren't serious before?

14:53.607 --> 14:55.107
Just watch how it's done.

14:57.697 --> 15:00.947
[♪ mystical music playing]

15:01.077 --> 15:02.117
Huh?

15:02.497 --> 15:03.747
Isn't that...

15:04.327 --> 15:06.287
[RUDEUS] Ever since Roxy
taught me lightning,

15:06.407 --> 15:08.627
I've been experimenting
with how to cast it.

15:09.167 --> 15:11.167
The key to this spell
is compression.

15:11.287 --> 15:13.047
You spread a ton of mana
through the sky

15:13.167 --> 15:14.297
to make some clouds,

15:14.417 --> 15:17.217
then compress them
to cause a lightning strike.

15:17.837 --> 15:20.797
So, if I can keep the clouds
small from the start,

15:21.347 --> 15:24.137
I'm able to fire off
a less powerful bolt.

15:24.977 --> 15:26.687
-I call it...
-[lightning strikes]

15:26.807 --> 15:27.767
...electric.

15:27.897 --> 15:31.477
[crackling]

15:31.817 --> 15:33.107
[both gasp]

15:38.317 --> 15:41.197
Well, I don't know about you,
but I think that's game!

15:41.327 --> 15:42.237
That's cheating!

15:42.367 --> 15:43.657
Magic? Come on!

15:43.787 --> 15:45.407
-She's not wrong.
-Rudy.

15:45.537 --> 15:47.707
that wasn't very mature,
even for you.

15:49.127 --> 15:50.167
Yeah.

15:53.587 --> 15:56.547
[AISHA] Looky, looky! Did you
see all the fish I caught?

15:56.667 --> 15:58.587
How'd you do today, Norn?

15:59.337 --> 16:01.097
Well, thanks to everything
Roxy taught me,

16:01.217 --> 16:03.967
I was able to catch
a giant fish really fast.

16:04.097 --> 16:05.007
[Aisha grumbles]

16:05.557 --> 16:08.557
Roxy, next time,
I want you to teach me.

16:08.687 --> 16:10.097
You caught
way more fish than I did.

16:10.227 --> 16:11.727
You don't need any more help.

16:11.857 --> 16:12.857
Roxy should stay with me

16:12.977 --> 16:14.727
because I actually need her,
unlike you.

16:14.857 --> 16:16.107
[Roxy chuckles] Oh, girls,

16:16.237 --> 16:17.777
there's no need
to fight over me.

16:17.897 --> 16:19.777
I'd be delighted
to teach you both.

16:20.407 --> 16:21.367
[door opens]

16:21.487 --> 16:22.987
[NORN, AISHA] Hey, we're home!

16:23.117 --> 16:24.577
That was so fun.

16:25.577 --> 16:27.747
Hey, happy birthday, ladies.

16:28.077 --> 16:29.957
[both gasp]

16:30.077 --> 16:31.997
[BOTH] Happy birthday
to you both.

16:32.127 --> 16:35.837
Okay, you know we already
turned 11, though, don't you?

16:35.957 --> 16:37.337
[SYLPHIETTE] Yeah, we know,

16:37.417 --> 16:40.177
but we didn't get to throw you
a party when you turned 10,

16:40.297 --> 16:41.847
so Rudy had an idea.

16:41.967 --> 16:43.927
He said, "What's wrong
with doing it a year late?"

16:44.047 --> 16:45.927
[AISHA] Did he really?

16:46.057 --> 16:47.597
Now, go in.

16:47.727 --> 16:49.687
[♪ gentle music playing]

16:53.647 --> 16:55.647
[both exclaiming]

16:55.767 --> 16:56.937
[Rudeus clears throat]

16:57.067 --> 17:00.067
Okay, everyone have
something to drink?

17:01.357 --> 17:04.157
It's been seven years
since the displacement.

17:04.657 --> 17:08.117
It took a while, but we're all
back together again.

17:08.657 --> 17:09.787
Dad is gone,

17:10.157 --> 17:12.417
and we don't know
if Mom will ever be the same,

17:13.327 --> 17:15.127
but you know as well as I do,

17:15.417 --> 17:17.627
Dad wouldn’t want us
to mourn forever.

17:18.667 --> 17:21.297
So tonight, to honor his legacy,

17:21.757 --> 17:23.137
we should smile again.

17:23.797 --> 17:25.557
When I reconnected
with Dad in Begaritt,

17:25.677 --> 17:28.097
I promised him
that I would throw a big party

17:28.217 --> 17:29.637
if we ever found each other.

17:31.887 --> 17:34.057
So let's cut loose
and enjoy ourselves,

17:34.187 --> 17:35.517
like Dad would've wanted.

17:38.277 --> 17:39.397
Here's to Paul.

17:39.527 --> 17:40.437
[LILIA, SYLPHIETTE, ROXY]
For Paul!

17:40.567 --> 17:41.777
[AISHA, NORN] For Dad!

17:44.367 --> 17:46.697
[SYLPHIETTE] Here,
from Rudy and us.

17:46.827 --> 17:48.197
Just a little present
for you both.

17:48.947 --> 17:51.327
We really hope that you like
the gifts we picked out.

17:52.037 --> 17:53.917
Thank you all so much.

17:59.547 --> 18:01.007
[gasps excitedly]

18:01.547 --> 18:02.877
Can I open my gift now?

18:03.007 --> 18:04.297
Yes, of course you can.

18:04.427 --> 18:05.427
[giggles excitedly]

18:06.347 --> 18:07.677
[both giggle excitedly]

18:08.927 --> 18:10.267
[BOTH] Mm.

18:15.267 --> 18:16.897
[both gasp]

18:17.017 --> 18:19.897
[both giggling]

18:20.027 --> 18:21.397
No way!

18:21.527 --> 18:24.277
Is that a new jacket?
Look, I got some boots!

18:24.397 --> 18:25.867
I'm happy for you.

18:25.987 --> 18:28.077
You both got wonderful presents.

18:28.197 --> 18:29.827
Hey, Mom, check it out!

18:29.947 --> 18:31.117
I got a nice present!

18:31.237 --> 18:34.617
I can wear it
next time we go out together.

18:34.957 --> 18:35.917
[both gasp]

18:36.037 --> 18:37.167
[gasps]

18:41.707 --> 18:44.007
Did, uh, she just smile?

18:46.717 --> 18:48.387
You're still in there.

18:48.507 --> 18:50.007
-[rustles]
-[gasps]

18:50.597 --> 18:52.427
[♪ gentle music playing]

18:53.137 --> 18:54.177
[giggles]

18:57.607 --> 19:00.437
My lady. Thank goodness.

19:00.937 --> 19:02.527
[sobs]

19:07.527 --> 19:10.617
Here, this is from my lady
and I for the two of you.

19:11.077 --> 19:13.787
[NORN] Oh, Lilia.
Thank you so much.

19:13.907 --> 19:17.207
[AISHA] Um, Mom,
are you sure I can have one too?

19:17.827 --> 19:19.877
Yes, of course you can, dear.

19:19.997 --> 19:22.497
You're Lord Paul's daughter too,
you know.

19:22.627 --> 19:24.127
You always will be.

19:25.127 --> 19:26.337
[sobs]

19:26.467 --> 19:28.887
Thank you, Mom, so, so much.

19:32.137 --> 19:35.887
My lady, I hope we'll have
many more good times together.

19:38.977 --> 19:40.017
[gasps]

19:46.397 --> 19:48.067
Thank you very much.

19:52.987 --> 19:54.787
-[RUDEUS] Roxy.
-Uh.

19:57.497 --> 19:59.577
Yes? You called me?

19:59.707 --> 20:02.627
Here, take it.
This one's from us to you.

20:02.747 --> 20:04.457
Huh? Oh.

20:04.587 --> 20:06.457
Uh, what for?

20:06.587 --> 20:08.047
It's a wedding present.

20:08.177 --> 20:11.137
Roxy, congratulations
on your marriage.

20:11.257 --> 20:12.807
I... I don't--

20:12.927 --> 20:14.427
Go on, just open it.

20:20.187 --> 20:21.437
[gasps]

20:22.187 --> 20:23.357
Is this...

20:23.897 --> 20:25.027
Listen,

20:25.527 --> 20:28.357
remember when I told you I got
really lucky to bump into Rudy?

20:28.737 --> 20:29.777
I do.

20:30.107 --> 20:33.077
If Rudy and I never
crossed paths again that day,

20:33.197 --> 20:35.237
well, I--
I don't think I'd be alive

20:35.367 --> 20:36.867
and in this room right now.

20:37.407 --> 20:38.747
That's an exaggeration.

20:38.867 --> 20:40.247
It's not, I promise.

20:40.877 --> 20:44.207
I'm grateful.
Meeting Rudy changed my life.

20:44.667 --> 20:45.877
It's true.

20:45.997 --> 20:48.217
And I'm so glad
someone who changed his life

20:48.337 --> 20:49.217
loves him too.

20:49.587 --> 20:52.217
I really don't care
if that person is me or not.

20:52.887 --> 20:54.137
[breathes shakily]

20:54.257 --> 20:56.137
And so, if I was the reason

20:56.267 --> 20:58.177
that Rudy
couldn't return those feelings,

20:58.307 --> 20:59.977
well then, I-- I don't know.

21:00.097 --> 21:01.437
It's all new to me.

21:02.057 --> 21:03.977
Oh, I can't find
the right words.

21:04.607 --> 21:05.687
[gasps]

21:06.527 --> 21:08.237
[SYLPHIETTE]
So I have a proposal.

21:09.397 --> 21:10.737
Come join us.

21:10.857 --> 21:13.157
You and I can be
like Zenith and Lilia.

21:15.617 --> 21:17.407
[crying]

21:18.367 --> 21:20.787
Thank you very much.

21:23.827 --> 21:26.837
[RUDEUS] We're all a big,
happy, smiling family.

21:27.587 --> 21:29.707
I'm sure this is
exactly the kind of life

21:29.837 --> 21:31.667
that Paul wanted for us.

21:38.097 --> 21:40.727
-One, two, three.
-Smile, Lucie!

21:41.597 --> 21:43.557
Aisha, what’s that face?

21:43.687 --> 21:45.937
[all laughing]

21:46.397 --> 21:47.857
-[LILIA] Master Rudeus.
-[ALL] Well, Rudy.

21:47.977 --> 21:50.527
From us to you,
happy fifth birthday!

21:52.147 --> 21:54.237
When the girls both turn 15,

21:54.367 --> 21:56.237
we'll throw 'em
another big party.

21:57.697 --> 21:59.367
Look, I think she's smiling.

21:59.487 --> 22:01.827
-Lucie!
-So cute!

22:01.957 --> 22:03.077
[all laughing]

22:04.827 --> 22:06.997
[♪ closing theme song playing]
